__REVIEW_PROFILE__

PROJECT CONTEXT — This project has two independent TypeScript codelines, both using vitest as the test runner and typescript in strict mode:
- mocka: fare-calculation logic. Ticket MOCK3-1 is a boundary bug where riders aged exactly 65 are charged the adult fare instead of the correct senior fare — the fix is an operator-boundary change (e.g. >= vs >), so scrutinise the comparison operator and confirm the test covers the exact boundary value (65) plus the values on either side (64, 66).
- mockb: schedule / departure-board rendering. Ticket MOCK3-2 is a loop-bound bug where the final stop is omitted from the departure board — the fix is a loop-bounds change, so scrutinise the loop condition (< vs <=, off-by-one on length) and confirm the test covers a stop list whose final entry is the one being dropped.
Both fixes are expected to be one- or two-line changes. A diff that adds new modules, new abstractions, or more than a handful of lines for either ticket is likely over-engineered — flag it under CONCISION & REUSE.

